# Owners of the licence boundary.
#
# Antgrid is dual-licensed by path (LICENSING.md): MPL-2.0 everywhere except
# relay/ and web/, which are Elastic-2.0. GitHub reports ONE licence for a
# repository — MPL-2.0, detected from the root LICENSE.md — and GitHub ToS D.6
# licenses a contribution under "the same terms" as that notice. An outside
# patch to an ELv2 directory would therefore arrive under terms that contradict
# the file it lands in, and nothing in either licence lets us relicense it.
#
# So these paths take maintainer review, and outside patches to them are refused
# outright: CONTRIBUTING.md states the policy and contribution-policy.yml
# enforces it. Ownership here is about licensing authority, not code review —
# add reviewers for that separately.
#
# packages/antgrid-wire is listed because relay/ and web/ both import it. A
# contribution there is MPL-2.0 permanently and can never cross the boundary,
# which is the same trap arriving from the other side.

/relay/                   @bharathm03
/web/                     @bharathm03
/packages/antgrid-wire/   @bharathm03

